	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="12"><b>Summary of trip to Kedge Keep.</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=27">Orion</a> - On June 11, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">After much uncertainty, and some hesitation 6 of us over 40 were able to get together for a little outing.<br><br>Clatene, Obino, Sdadar, Speechlessag, Trowsk and myself(as Abyena) were finally able to work everything out and get together for a rather successful trip deep into Kedge keep.<br><br>We started out by heading down and cleared out of the minor spawns, to let everyone get their bearings, and then continued to slay sharks, and kick some mermaid tail! In the end we ended not only clearing bubble's den, but all the mobs in the area and cleared Esterella's temple!<br><br>Unfortunatly, after this it was getting late, and Speechlessag had to go to get some rest, with everyone else getting a tad weary as well. So we decided to give one rare a try and headed off to smite the shark, Cauldronboil, we were doing quite well! But, as luck would have it, we were forced to give up when he was down to a mere fraction of his health with a vow that we will return soon, and finish what we started!<br><br>All in all, a great job by all! Its not easy getting used to fighting underwater! I had lots of fun, and i do believe that everyone else did as well.<br>Let Kedge be warned! We WILL be back!</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="11"><b>Zone Guide launched</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - On June 7, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">I have added a VERY useful tool to the site.<br><br>The <a href="hunting.asp">Zone Guide</a> will let you know what to do in zones and what zones you should be at for your level.<br><br>Only members can add to it but all can benefit. I will make a link for it in the menu when I redesign it.</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="10"><b>RE:Dark Elf Corruptor goes down 5 times.</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=24">Nolil</a> - On May 29, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">The guild had 5 members that needed the drop for their druid/ranger epic from the DE Corruptor in east karana. He went down 5 times in a tad over 7 hours on  memorial day weekend, Sunday. In addition, the two dark reavers that spawn were killed everytime. Two of the spawns, triggered, no deaths were involved the other three times, approx. 5 people died altogeter.<br>There were many members present at this event. Thanks to all of you. This is another sign of the growth of this guild. Very Good job guild. Keep on keeping on.<br><br>In addition, Tarbul is now a piece of cake. He went down several times. Aaldaar looted the drop for his epic quest.<br>Nolil</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="9"><b>Well Done Drakkon's!</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=18">Horseman</a> - On May 21, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">The guild has chalked up our first major kill.  Tarbul Earthstrider, the named Hill Giant in EK has fallen, and with a loud thump, he landed flat on his face. <br> His drop was an item for the Mage Epic. <br> With a well planned out attack and all members of the group doing there tasks set before battle to perfection, for a mob that of that stature, we took very little damage.  Nice work to Treowe, Sdadar, Glaur, Jammer, and Naeeren.  Brotherlogain was the receipient of his drop and he shall fall again for others.  He was the first big kill and more will soon follow.  Well Done!</td>
	</tr>
	
	<tr>
		<td bgcolor="#800000" colspan="3"><a name="8"><b>Screenshot Gallery up!</b></a> <font size="-2">Posted by <a href="members.asp?PlayerID=23">Matrim</a> - On May 11, 2001</font></td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td colspan="3">I have added a cool new feature to the site. Send me your screenshots from in game and I'll host them in the gallery.<br><br>Please tell me the 'section' the screen shots belong in and only send in quality shots. Don't zip all of your screenshots and send them to me. I don't want to sort through them and see which shots are good.<br><br>New sections will be added as the topics arise but for now we have Scenic and Humor. If you want your character screenshot hosted please send that as well and you can make it your profile image. If we get enough profile images I may make a section for all of them so the guild can be seen on the same page.<br><br>Also, you can send me a description for each picture that will be displayed under the full image.</td>
	</tr>
	
